# Set 2 · The Difficult Paper

> About 70% difficult and 30% medium: theory-heavy, cross-topic questions that reward depth.

Five of the seven Part II questions are **difficult** — historicizing constructionism, men's feminism, the gendered political economy of adjustment, honour killing through Galtung, and the "Western import" debate — and two are **medium** (family law; the notes on governance and world-system theory). Of the twenty MCQs, **fourteen are difficult and six medium**: lesser-known thinkers, "which is NOT" items and keys of "None of these".

